    "word_count": 51,
    "html": "<p>Melina Stamoulis is an Australian businesswoman from the family behind Gold Medal soft drinks and Stamoulis Property Group. The daughter of Spiros and Helen Stamoulis, she worked with her parents and brother Harry as the family expanded into property investment. She has also participated in its Greek-language media businesses in Melbourne.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Melina Stamoulis has helped oversee Melbourne's Hellenic Museum, established by her father in memory of her sister Nafsika. Housed in the former Royal Mint, the museum presents ancient and contemporary Greek culture through exhibitions, workshops and performances. The Stamoulis family continues to support it as lifetime trustees.\n\nHer family's cultural work also reaches listeners through 3XY Radio Hellas. Alongside her brother Harry and mother Eleni, she has helped continue the station's work after her father's death. Its round-the-clock Greek-language service combines news and music with community programming, and its broadcasts support charitable fundraising.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 88,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Historical museum involvement is reported independently; present institution purpose and family support are primary. Her continuing radio involvement is explicitly named in the owner's anniversary speech."
    },
    "source_ids": [
